Package: bewrs
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Early-Warning Risk Surveillance for Healthcare
        Performance Monitoring
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R: 
    person("Muhammad Zahir", "Khan", , "zahirstat007@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides Bayesian early-warning surveillance methods for
    monitoring healthcare performance and patient safety outcomes.
    The package draws on risk-adjusted monitoring frameworks developed by
    Steiner et al. (2000) <doi:10.1093/biostatistics/1.4.441>,
    Spiegelhalter et al. (2003) <doi:10.1002/sim.1546>, Cook et al.
    (2011) <doi:10.1136/bmjqs.2008.031831>, and Neuburger et al. (2017)
    <doi:10.1136/bmjqs-2016-005511>. The package implements Bayesian
    predictive modelling, risk-adjusted monitoring, early-warning signal
    detection, and graphical tools for continuous quality improvement
    and healthcare performance assessment.
